{
  "change": "Win32 Mesa shader cache avoids retrying a missing file and sorts entries only during actual eviction. The file format, cache namespace, integrity validation and shared-size reconciliation are preserved.",
  "tested_backend": "Real disk_cache_get(), disk_cache_create_custom(), and local Vulkan ICDs on Switch Lite with Code 0 and AC Handheld.",
  "methods": {
    "filesystem": "768 deterministic distinct missing keys and 768 valid blobs. Four old and four new processes in ABBA/BAAB order per architecture used the same populated isolated directory. Each process verified all 768 hits byte-for-byte and opened the under-budget directory eight more times. Per-entry times are process batch averages. Open percentiles describe the 32 observed opens.",
    "graphics": "24 draws per process on the matched GM20B LUID, checking 1024 reference pixels and two 64-byte guards every time. Absent shader cache for cold process, same entries in warm sibling. First comparison used the existing installed baseline and newly signed candidate. Second comparison used freshly relinked and signed versions of both sources under sibling directories, identical DLL basenames. Host PE normalization verified that each pair of like-source unsigned images matched after removing linker timestamp fields. No system translation-cache flush.",
    "interpretation": "Pipeline creation is reported independently of filesystem lookup. Neither a cache lookup speedup nor a change in a 32x32 offscreen fixture establishes a game FPS improvement.",
    "thermal": "The controller verified AC online, Handheld, GPU Code 0 and active DFLL. Instantaneous clocks remained dynamic; their before/after samples are in the graphics table.",
    "pipeline_cpu": "GetProcessTimes kernel plus user CPU time for the whole process during vkCreateGraphicsPipelines. Worker threads may run concurrently. CPU clocks before and after are outside the entire offscreen process, not inside its pipeline interval."
  },
