  "findings": {
    "missing_keys": "The median of four per-process batch averages decreased on all three architectures. The 768 hits in every batch matched the bytes put by the seeding process.",
    "first_use": "With a freshly relinked DLL on each side, the first observed x86 and x64 cold pipelines were slower with the candidate by 116.31 ms and 114.96 ms respectively. Each first-use observation is a single sample for that image. Both builds also paid a first-use cost relative to later cold starts. The experiment does not isolate the reason for the difference.",
    "repeat_runs": "Excluding the first pair from each fresh image leaves three cold and three warm observations per build and architecture. All observations, including the first pair, are in the CSV. A game frame-rate gain has not been established."
  },
  "x64_dxvk_game_comparison": {
    "scene": "FTEQW, LibreQuake lq_e0m1, 640 x 360, x64 DXVK D3D9 on GM20B, one fresh game directory per image. Candidate ran first in the completed pair. A verified title-bar activation was available in both runs. Both image binaries had been exercised by the prior offscreen experiment.",
    "measurement": "Each phase used foreground movement and observed game-PID Win32k producer events and DWM event 46 attributed to the game window. One session per version, adaptive clocks. FPS capture in Pacecar remained off in both sessions. The first setup attempt stopped before starting the game while trying to toggle Pacecar. KMD preemption samples are system-wide boundary observations, including DWM. They do not measure time spent in a stage or isolate the game context.",
    "game_selection_after_run": "Original loader settings restored and hash-verified after trials. Both temporary executable aliases retired.",
